Hug...

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:37.250
HUG...

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.040
Oh no.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.660
I don't know if I'll be able to keep my cool about this...

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.830
Tsutsui, who turns to dating sims in order to understand a woman's mind

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:50.790
Maiko

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.080
Sorry... I decided to date my senpai.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:50.910
But why?!

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:54.910
I did the thoroughly suggestive things,
so which choice was wrong?!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.540
A woman's mind is too difficult!
It's a game, but I'm still shocked!

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.750
Because I'll be transferring schools in half a year.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:06.700
Well... will I just get mad when we break up?

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.580
I wonder where in the world
my energy is going to go then...

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.660
And I still don't know about when to call her.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.250
Really, I don't understand that boy.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.330
Tsutsui, are you trying to move on to a new genre?

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.700
Like maybe an otaku guy in a girls' dating sim?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.790
What's that? It sounds lame.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.200
Arisa!

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:34.950
Shun-kun!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.620
Arisa, you're cute, just like a dog!

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:39.500
What?

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.450
Lend me some money.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.580
Wait a sec, 'kay? I wonder how much I have...

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:46.910
Isn't that type of thing bad?

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:51.160
Well, I don't think this is something
we should interfere with, though.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.330
But... I see. Okay.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.160
Igarashi?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.790
I knew it! This is Igarashi from class C.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.500
I know. You're well-known for a lot of things, huh?

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.080
Igarashi is a really good person!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.000
You don't know me that well, do you?

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:15.040
That's true... But I can understand that
from just talking to you a bit!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.450
That's great, Arisa! You're making more friends!

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.290
We are not friends.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:20.040
Huh?

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:23.120
Right! She said she doesn't need friends.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.080
Bye. See you at school.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.750
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:32.120
Tsutsui, you're really amazing
when you get into something.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.700
You've got an inquiring mind.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:37.660
Even now, I don't really get how
to show my affection towards you.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.410
Huh?

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.120
It's kinda good for when things get all pent up.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.660
Wait... What did I say just now?

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.080
Seriously?!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.370
Yeah. I forgot that I left another girls' clothes in my room, man.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:52.250
She noticed, but she didn't say anything.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.370
For real, Ishino is so convenient!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.290
She's real put-together, right?

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:01.250
I hate when people are saying cruel things!
Let's go over there, Tsutsui!

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.370
Y-yeah...

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.830
I-Ishino!

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.580
I'm an idiot, huh?

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.160
You're wondering why I like someone like that, right?

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:16.790
I can say "Even so, I still like him" and end this, right?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.250
When it comes to the type of person,

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.660
other people can think whatever they want, right?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.540
When it's the type of love
that has people wondering why,

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:30.000
I think that if it makes you happy, then that's fine.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.830
The type of love
that has people
wondering why

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:35.870
Man, and she gives me money,
so it's hard to break it off, ya know!

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:38.000
Good thing she's a stupid girl, right?

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.790
Let's go, Ishino.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:41.660
Huh?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:45.500
SMASH

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.250
What are you doing?!

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:51.540
What you're saying and what you're doing are different!

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.330
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:55.500
I couldn't really hold myself back.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.620
Sorry! I'm really not trying to intervene or anything!

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.620
I personally just got really pissed off.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:04.160
If you're happy, Ishino, I think it's okay.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.080
Bye.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:12.700
Do you think I'm stupid too, Tsutsui?

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:17.660
I understand the feeling you have
of liking someone that much.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:22.870
But, in a manga or a game, people like that
are not good characters in general.

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:30.410
You listened to my problems. The Ishino that
simply listened to someone like me, is a good person.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:34.330
I don't want you to get the bad ending....
is what I'm thinking.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.540
Sorry, but we gotta go chase after her.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.040
You broke up?

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.660
Yeah. After all that, he was really mad.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:51.910
Should... I go apologize to him?

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:55.330
I'm okay with this.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.200
Hey, don't cry! It's really distressing!

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.910
A hanky, a hanky!

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:06.330
But I'm not happy! Not at all!

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:12.700
I couldn't think something like "Even so, I'm happy!"

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.750
Alright! We're going to the roof!

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:16.450
Huh?

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:20.160
Plain
Powdered sugar
Chocolate
Strawberry

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.120
I made cheesecake and donuts for today.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.120
Plain

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:23.790
The sweets are... sinking in.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:30.000
When you eat sweets, the secreted serotonin
is effective for calming and stress reduction.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.330
It's good to eat a lot.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.040
You've got something...

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:39.660
Up to now I haven't been the slightest bit jealous
that Tstusui is your boyfriend,

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.000
but right now I'm jealous!

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:46.290
Why are there only honest girls like this around me?

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:49.830
It's okay. Ishino isn't a good judge of character,

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:53.910
but she's great at finding
the good things in people, for sure.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.870
Something else will surely appear, so it's okay.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:04.700
I really don't get it.
Huh? Um... I don't have female friends...

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.120
Huh? Um... I don't have female friends...

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.040
I wonder what I should do.
I know that!

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:11.080
I understand people's emotions even less now. But...

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:16.120
Today, at any rate, I'm kinda glad I'm a bit of a normie.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.870
Tsutsui, the strawberry one is delicious, too!
